@startuml
title Financing Service Overview

interface FS_API
package "Financing Service" {
    FS_API - [FinancingService] : provides
    [Chain-Gang\n(BSV library)]
    [uls-client\n(mapi-lite client)]
    file "configuration\n(financing-service.toml)" as fs_toml

    [FinancingService] ..> fs_toml : read at startup
}

cloud "Blockchain" {
}

[FinancingService] ..> [Chain-Gang\n(BSV library)] : chain reads\n(and broadcast by default)

[FinancingService] ..> [uls-client\n(mapi-lite client)] : broadcast\n<<optional: [mapi_lite]>>

[Chain-Gang\n(BSV library)] ..> [WhatsOnChain] : WoC interface\n(interface_type = woc)

[Chain-Gang\n(BSV library)] ..> [UTXO as a Service\n(UaaS)] : UaaS interface\n(interface_type = uaas)\n<<optional>>

[Chain-Gang\n(BSV library)] ..> [Bitcoin node\n(JSON-RPC)] : RPC interface\n(interface_type = rpc)\n<<optional>>

[uls-client\n(mapi-lite client)] ..> [mapi-lite] : POST /mapi/txs\nGET /mapi/feeQuote (health)

[WhatsOnChain] ..> Blockchain
[UTXO as a Service\n(UaaS)] ..> Blockchain
[Bitcoin node\n(JSON-RPC)] ..> Blockchain
[mapi-lite] ..> Blockchain

note bottom of fs_toml
  One blockchain interface is selected at startup via
  [blockchain_interface].interface_type (woc, uaas, rpc or test)
  and serves chain reads. Funding transactions are broadcast
  through it too, unless a [mapi_lite] section is present, in
  which case they go to mapi-lite and GET /ready probes it.
end note

@enduml
